Explanation

This program performs graph traversal using two methods:

1. Depth First Search (DFS)
DFS explores the graph deeply first.
It uses recursion.
It visits a node, then moves to its unvisited neighbor.

Working:

Start from a given vertex.
Mark it as visited.
Recursively visit all unvisited neighbors.
2. Breadth First Search (BFS)
BFS explores the graph level by level.
It uses a queue (FIFO).

Working:

Start from a vertex.
Mark it visited and add to queue.
Remove from queue and visit neighbors.
Repeat until queue is empty.
Functions Used
add_edge() → adds edge to graph
dfs_recursive() → performs DFS
bfs() → performs BFS
Output
Displays DFS traversal (recursive)
